# Normalise line endings: LF in the repo, LF on checkout everywhere (silences GitHub Desktop's CRLF warning).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git LFS — big binary files live outside the repo's history (added 2026-09-14).
#
# Why: git keeps every version of every file forever. That is free for text and expensive for art.
# 156 building sprites is 33 MB, and it is the SMALLEST the art will ever be — map tiles, ~60
# portrait layers, units and ships are still to come. Adding LFS later means rewriting history,
# so it goes in now.
#
# These lines replace the plain `*.png binary` entries that were here before: `filter=lfs` moves the
# bytes to LFS, and the `-text` on each line keeps the "do not touch line endings" behaviour that
# `binary` was providing. Fonts stay plain `binary` — there are few of them and they are small.
#
# Note: a handful of PNGs committed before this date (the old three-stage sprites) stay in history
# as ordinary blobs. Converting them would mean rewriting history for a few megabytes, which is not
# worth it. Everything from here is LFS.

*.png  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.psd  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ogg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

*.ttf binary
